  body: |
    # SPC claimant temporary absence in the source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The guidance describes different temporary-absence limits for an SPC claimant, conditional on expected duration, other entitlement conditions and specified exceptions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 077001 refers to conditional four-, eight- and twenty-six-week cases. The death-related exception at 077002 and the treatment conditions at 077003 must not be replaced by a single universal limit. Current regulations and individual outcomes remain unreviewed.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 077001, PDF page 8](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6426e57e7de82b000c3133eb/dmg-ch07-06.pdf#page=8)
    - [DMG 077002, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6426e57e7de82b000c3133eb/dmg-ch07-06.pdf#page=9)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:20.305518Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication or legal commencement date. The attachment publication date is not established by the frozen metadata. Source-stated dates require their own role and precision.

