    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source supplies separate claimant-payment and household-membership provisions, each with its own exception references.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0008
      quote: "077001 SPC can continue to be paid whilst a claimant is temporarily absent from GB 1 if the other\nconditions of entitlement continue to be satisfied and the absence is no longer than\n\n\n1. 4 weeks where the absence is not expected to exceed 4 weeks2 or\n\n\n2. 8 weeks3 where paragraph 077002 applies or\n\n\n3. 26 weeks4 where paragraph 077003 applies.\n\n\nNote: See DMG 04642 for effective dates for supersession.\n\n\n                                                 1 SPC Regs, reg 3; 2 reg 3(1)(a); 3 reg 3(1)(b); 4 reg 3(1)(c)\n\n\nExample 1\n\n\nJason notifies the DM that he is going abroad for 3 weeks. The DM decides that he remains entitled for\nthose 3 weeks. He contracts food poisoning and has to extend his stay by a further 2 weeks. As Jason’s"
      locator: DMG 077001
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part6/0011
      quote: "077005 A person is treated as being a member of the claimant’s household whilst temporarily absent\n\nfrom GB1 if the absence is no longer than\n\n\n1. 4 weeks where the absence is not expected to exceed 4 weeks2or\n\n\n2. 8 weeks3 where paragraph 077006 applies or\n\n\n3. 26 weeks4 where paragraph 077007 applies.\n\n\n                                            1 SPC Regs, reg 5(1)(f); 2 Reg 5(1A)(a); 3 reg 5(1A)(b); 4 reg 5(1A)\n\n\n\nThe 8 week rule"
      locator: DMG 077005
